<title>CHINA: Bombardier says China to buy 5 aircraft.</title>
<headline>Bombardier says China to buy 5 aircraft.</headline>
<dateline>BEIJING 1997-01-22</dateline>
<text>
<p>China has signed a deal with Bombardier Inc to buy five corporate jets for a total of $116 million, the Canadian company said on Wednesday.  </p>
<p>Bombardier said China would take delivery of three of the Canadair corporate jets this year and the other two in 1998.</p>
<p>The agreement also includes pilot and maintenance training, spare parts, it said.</p>
<p>The deal was signed with Poly Techologies, a purchasing agency of the Chinese government that also handles military procurement, and China United Airlines, a military owned carrier that will operate the planes.</p>
</text>
